.TH SDL_TextureAddressMode 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_TextureAddressMode \- The addressing mode for a texture when used in
.BR SDL_RenderGeometry ().

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_render.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef enum SDL_TextureAddressMode
.BI "{
.BI "    SDL_TEXTURE_ADDRESS_INVALID = -1,
.BI "    SDL_TEXTURE_ADDRESS_AUTO,   /**< Wrapping is enabled if texture coordinates are outside [0, 1], this is the default */
.BI "    SDL_TEXTURE_ADDRESS_CLAMP,  /**< Texture coordinates are clamped to the [0, 1] range */
.BI "    SDL_TEXTURE_ADDRESS_WRAP    /**< The texture is repeated (tiled) */
.BI "} SDL_TextureAddressMode;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This affects how texture coordinates are interpreted outside of [0, 1]
.PP
Texture wrapping is always supported for power of two texture sizes, and is supported for other texture sizes if
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_TEXTURE_WRAPPING_BOOLEAN
is set to true\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This enum is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

